The 5906-symbol word in data/superperm7_5906.txt was found by Greg Egan and Robin Houston (February 2019);
it is the file 7_5906_nsk666646664466646666_2SYMM_FS.txt published on Egan's page
(https://www.gregegan.net/SCIENCE/Superpermutations/Superpermutations.html) and in the public
Superpermutators corpus (https://github.com/superpermutators/superperm).  It is data, included so that
the headline statement is two-sided, and no claim of originality is made for it.

This product depends on, but does not include, Lean 4 (https://github.com/leanprover/lean4) and mathlib4
(https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4) with its standard dependency set (batteries, aesop, Qq,
ProofWidgets4, import-graph, LeanSearchClient, plausible: Apache License 2.0; Cli: MIT License), fetched by
the build tool at the revisions pinned in lake-manifest.json.
